. // Bayesian design      
. // 90% power for 80-20 evidence
. // Assumes benefit of better treatment = 5%
. bayespower, n1(890) n0(890) priorspec(ms) ///
>         prior1d(.55 0) prior0d(.50 0) ///
>         prior1a(.50 .29) prior0a(.50 .29) ///
>         seed(3) cutoff(.80) 
--------------------------- PROBLEM --------------------------
                                          Group 1    Group 0
Sample size                               890        890
Design prior:   mean                      .55        .5
                SD                        0          0
Analysis prior: mean                      .5         .5
                SD                        .29        .29
Margin                                               0
Power is p(evidence of benefit...         AND true benefit)
--------------------------------------------------------------

--------------------------- RESULTS ------------------------------------------------
Cut-off                                   Value      95% Monte Carlo intl  Frequent.
Mean post. prob. of benefit               .93334258  .93101914  .93566602
Power for post. prob. of benefit > .8     .9026      .89662086  .90834347  .89833441
